# Paths the published Comfy Registry archive does not need.
#
# `comfy node publish` zips every git-tracked file minus these patterns
# (gitwildmatch, the .gitignore syntax); `[tool.comfy].includes` in
# pyproject.toml forces a path back in. Keeping dev tooling out shrinks a
# ComfyUI-Manager install and leaves the registry's security scan looking at
# shipped code only.
#
# What stays: __init__.py, src/, web/, assets/ (the README's icon),
# pyproject.toml (registry metadata), README.md (shown by Manager),
# CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE.

# Dev tooling and CI
.comfyignore
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
scripts/
tests/
Makefile
tidy.sh

# Dev environment pins; the pack itself has no runtime dependencies
uv.lock
.python-version
.gitignore

# Agent-facing docs; README.md is the human-facing guide and ships
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
